Devin, you asked which document to model against and the answer is narrower t=
han you might like. Model against the executed instrument and nothing else.

There are four term sheet artefacts circulating: an unsigned draft, a redline=
 showing proposed changes to that draft, a competing indicative proposal from=
 another party, and the exhibit attached to the executed version. Only one of=
 those four is signed, and a redline is a record of what somebody asked for, =
not a record of what they got.

The specific risk is the purchaser top-up right that appears in the redline. =
It reads as though it survived. It did not, and I have checked the signature =
pages rather than relying on the file name.

Talia, since you are building the register, please cite the document by its s=
ignature date rather than by its version number. Version numbers are the leas=
t reliable thing in that folder.

